WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.135
-Hey, everyone!
Thank you very, very much.

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:04.671
And welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.005
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:07.073
Well, guys, this morning,

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.642
the Commission on
Presidential Debates,

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.677
which I'm assuming is
just a bunch of guys with

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:16.382
bird masks and butt paddles,
made a big announcement

00:00:16.382 --> 00:00:17.449
about the
next presidential debate.

00:00:17.449 --> 00:00:18.784
Listen to this.

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:21.120 line:0%
-The commission just announcing
that the next debate

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.124 line:0%
will be entirely virtual as the
president still battles COVID.

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:28.561 line:0%
The candidates will participate
from separate remote locations.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:31.064
-Yeah, a virtual debate...

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:34.200
with two guys in their 70s
and a moderator in his 60s.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.170
I'm sure that'll
run real smooth.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:39.505
And to make it
even more annoying,

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:40.706
they're going to have
Trump and Biden

00:00:40.706 --> 00:00:42.475
chomp on baby carrots
while they talk.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:46.746
[ Chomping ]

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.147
A virtual debate with Trump?

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:49.515
Come on.
How great would that be?

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:53.152
It's like, "Melania,
what's the Wi-Fi password?"

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:54.387
[ Slovenian accent ]
1, 2, 3, 4 --

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:59.526
same as nuke codes."

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:02.461
[ Normal voice ] Yeah, a virtual
debate seems like a safe idea.

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:04.296
During a phone call this morning
on "Fox Business,"

00:01:04.296 --> 00:01:06.665
Trump was asked about it,
and here's what he had to say.

00:01:06.665 --> 00:01:09.402 line:0%
-The CPD, the Commission
on Presidential Debates,

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:10.903 line:0%
announcing this morning

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:13.439 line:0%
that the second presidential
debate will be virtual.

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:15.942 line:0%
Are you saying
you're not going to participate?

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:26.685
-Yep, Trump says
he won't waste time.

00:01:26.685 --> 00:01:31.291
Then he went back to chatting on
Fox Business for 55 minutes.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.726
55 minutes.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.428
Halfway through,
Maria Bartiromo texted

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:36.729
the hosts of
"Fox &amp; Friends" like,

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:39.365
"How do you make him stop?"

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:40.933
Seriously, the call
was so exhausting,

00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:46.339
Maria went online and booked
four days at Walter Reed.

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.674
After Trump stated that
he would not "waste his time,"

00:01:48.674 --> 00:01:50.009
Joe Biden announced that he was

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:52.211
backing out of
the debate, as well.

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:53.479
It's like a group text.

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:54.914
Once one person bails on brunch,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.749
the floodgates open,
and everybody jumps ship.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:58.284
They're like,
"Uh, I got something, too.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:01.353
Yeah, yeah. Sorry.
Well, I forgot about that."

00:02:01.353 --> 00:02:02.755
It's too bad for the people
who were going to speak

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:03.956
at the town hall,
'cause they were

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:05.624
really looking forward
to having their questions

00:02:05.624 --> 00:02:08.628
ignored on national television.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.096
Anyway, back to
Trump's phone call.

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:11.897
Maria asked the president
how he's doing,

00:02:11.897 --> 00:02:13.499
and it was clear that Trump
is having a tough time

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:14.633
staying in quarantine.

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:15.735
Listen to this.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:28.948
-A rally?
He's actually considering that?

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:30.383
Trump's aides were like,
"You got it, boss,"

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:34.253
then put him in a room with
5,000 cardboard cutouts.

00:02:34.253 --> 00:02:35.587
Later in the interview,

00:02:35.587 --> 00:02:37.723
Trump had a sound bite
that I found very interesting.

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:38.758
Check this out.

00:02:51.937 --> 00:02:53.406
-[ As Trump ] Whaaat?

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:56.309
Wha...

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:57.343
I've never felt better.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:03:01.413
My body is a finely tuned
Swiss clock.

00:03:01.413 --> 00:03:03.649
Everything is in
perfect working order.

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:04.650
[ Normal voice ]
"So happy you're better."

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.987
[ As Trump ] Whaaat?

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.622
[ Normal voice ] Trump suddenly
turned into every grandpa

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:11.023
when you ask
how they're feeling.

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:13.092
"What?"

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.360
Also, minor detail --
there's no such thing

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.396
as being immune to COVID.

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:19.265
After he said that,
Dr. Fauci poured himself

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:23.269
a big antibody cocktail
minus the antibody.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.670
Towards the
end of the interview,

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.239
Maria had a question about
Trump's current COVID status,

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:28.741
and he gave her a
pretty interesting answer.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.075
Listen to this.

00:03:30.075 --> 00:03:32.711 line:0%
-You're feeling good.
Have you been tested recently?

00:03:32.711 --> 00:03:36.149 line:0%
Can you tell us anything else
about your condition?

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:41.821
-Essentially?

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.856
This is kind of
a binary situation.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.659
You either have COVID
or you don't.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:47.893
Doctors don't say, "Good news.

00:03:47.893 --> 00:03:51.964
You don't have COVID anymore...
more or less.

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:53.533
Per se."

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:54.968
That's not very comforting.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:57.236
You don't see a celebrity coming
out of rehab like, "All good.

00:03:57.236 --> 00:04:00.906
I'm essentially clean."

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:02.275
Well, guys, last night
was, of course,

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:04.143
the big vice-presidential
debate between

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:05.912
Mike Pence and Kamala Harris,

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.547
and everyone's
still talking about it

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:11.050
because a fly
actually landed on Pence's head.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.184
Watch this.
-Yes.

00:04:12.184 --> 00:04:16.288
-It's a great insult
to the men and women

00:04:16.288 --> 00:04:17.690
who serve in law enforcement.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:22.228
-Part of a pattern of
Donald Trump's.

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:23.296
He was...

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:26.198
-At that point,
every American was like,

00:04:26.198 --> 00:04:30.269
"Is that on him or on my TV?"

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:32.071
You know vice-presidential
debates are boring

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:36.809
when a fly shows up and the
entire Internet loses its mind.

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.745
Meanwhile, a bunch of other
flies off-camera were like,

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:39.879
"Oh, my God.

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:41.747
I can't believe
you actually did it!

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:44.684
You're a legend, dude!

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.486
Epic!

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:50.089
I can't believe you did it!"

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:52.258
Kamala Harris was probably
sitting there thinking,

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:53.793
"I've been
strong and commanding,

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:55.561
and all anyone is
going to be talking about

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:58.197
is that stupid fly."

00:04:58.197 --> 00:04:59.798
Yeah, that was
a tough moment for Pence,

00:04:59.798 --> 00:05:01.100
although it's still not
as bad as

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.668
the last
vice-presidential debate,

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:05.672
when a barn owl attacked
Tim Kaine.

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:10.409
Yep, Pence had a rough night.

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:12.878
As if the fly wasn't bad enough,
people also noticed

00:05:12.878 --> 00:05:15.081
there was something
going on with his eyeball.

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:16.215
Look at his eye.

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:21.020
Yeah, he's the head of
the Coronavirus Task Force.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.354
Not really a great look when

00:05:22.354 --> 00:05:27.760
you're covered in bugs
and bleeding out of your eye.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.862
Yep, last night's debate
was an epic battle

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:33.232
between side-eye and red-eye.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:34.867
It's a tough break for Pence.

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:36.902
It's hard to shake
the reputation of being robotic

00:05:36.902 --> 00:05:40.139
when you show up looking like
the Terminator.

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:41.541
Also, can you believe
Kamala Harris

00:05:41.541 --> 00:05:43.575
had to stare at that
for 90 minutes?

00:05:43.575 --> 00:05:45.011
As if she wasn't under
enough pressure,

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:48.514
she had to debate the Bond
villain with the leaky eye.

00:05:50.215 --> 00:05:52.952
[ As Le Chiffre ]
Be very careful, Mr. Bond.

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:54.320
[ Normal voice ]
People are worried about Pence

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:56.855
because pinkeye is a possible
symptom of coronavirus.

00:05:56.855 --> 00:05:58.124
Even scarier, today,

00:05:58.124 --> 00:06:03.729
Pence's temperature
shot all the way up to 84.6.

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:05.331
Well, a lot of people also
noticed that Pence

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:07.200
kept interrupting Harris,
but she wasn't having it.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.334
Watch this.

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:09.569 line:0%
-This is important, and I want
to add --

00:06:09.569 --> 00:06:10.602 line:0%
-Susan, I have to weigh in here.

00:06:10.602 --> 00:06:11.637 line:0%
-Mr. Vice President,
I'm speaking.

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:13.072 line:0%
-I have to weigh in.
-I'm speaking.

00:06:13.072 --> 00:06:15.207 line:0%
...raise taxes on anybody who
makes less than $400,000 a year.

00:06:15.207 --> 00:06:17.042 line:0%
-He said he's going to repeal
the Trump tax cuts.

00:06:17.042 --> 00:06:19.278 line:0%
-Mr. Vice President,
I'm speaking.

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.913 line:0%
-Well --
-I'm speaking.

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:23.149 line:0%
If you don't mind letting
me finish,

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:25.051 line:0%
we can then
have a conversation, okay?

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:26.218 line:0%
-Please.
-Okay.

00:06:26.218 --> 00:06:27.453 line:0%
In 1864 --

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:28.787 line:0%
-Well, I'd like you
to answer the question.

00:06:28.787 --> 00:06:30.823 line:0%
-Mr. Vice President,
I'm speaking.

00:06:30.823 --> 00:06:32.691 line:0%
I'm speaking. Okay?

00:06:32.691 --> 00:06:38.698
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:06:38.698 --> 00:06:40.332
-Compared to
the presidential debate,

00:06:40.332 --> 00:06:42.534
that wasn't too bad,
although that's like comparing

00:06:42.534 --> 00:06:45.671
a five-star restaurant to
a Waffle House at 3:00 a.m.

00:06:47.005 --> 00:06:48.674
That's right -- there were
a lot of memorable moments

00:06:48.674 --> 00:06:50.843
during the debate, and there are
plenty of jokes to be made,

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:52.778
but if it's alright,
I want to take a moment

00:06:52.778 --> 00:06:55.080
to say something serious
about democracy.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.282
That okay?

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:59.818
-You asking me?
I mean, it's your show, man.

00:06:59.818 --> 00:07:02.188
You can do whatever you want.

00:07:02.188 --> 00:07:06.659
-America is at an
inflection point right now.

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:10.195
And we, as a nation, have to
come together to make a choice.

00:07:10.195 --> 00:07:14.867
-[ Laughs ] Um, Jimmy,
you got something on your, uh...

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:18.904
-This country needs to
ask itself some hard questions,

00:07:18.904 --> 00:07:21.039
like, "What is America?

00:07:21.039 --> 00:07:22.808
Who is freedom?

00:07:22.808 --> 00:07:26.078
And when is liberty?"

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:28.981
-That didn't even make --
You know what?

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:32.117
I don't care, man.
Just keep doing your thing.

00:07:32.117 --> 00:07:34.153
-So get out there

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:37.390
and be the change
you want to see in the world.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:38.825
-Jimmy...

00:07:38.825 --> 00:07:42.228
-Uh, yeah? What's up, Tariq?
Something you want to tell me?

00:07:42.228 --> 00:07:46.999
-I just wanted to say
that was beautiful.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:56.842
-You trim your beard
or something?

00:07:56.842 --> 00:07:58.177
You look different.

00:07:58.177 --> 00:07:59.611
-No, man.

00:07:59.611 --> 00:08:02.181
There's a [bleep]
squirrel on my head.

00:08:13.158 --> 00:08:14.227
-Well, listen to this.

00:08:14.227 --> 00:08:16.028
I saw that
the governor of California

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:17.997
has a new recommendation
for residents

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:21.000
to safely eat at restaurants
during the pandemic.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.901 line:0%
-The governor's office
tweeted out, saying,

00:08:22.901 --> 00:08:24.971 line:0%
when you're eating out
at a restaurant,

00:08:24.971 --> 00:08:28.373 line:0%
to keep your mask on
in between bites of food.

00:08:28.373 --> 00:08:31.643 line:0%
The tweet even shows an image
of someone wearing a mask,

00:08:31.643 --> 00:08:33.946 line:0%
then not wearing a mask,
taking a bite,

00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:35.781 line:0%
and then putting
the mask back on again.

00:08:35.781 --> 00:08:37.717
-So you have to
pull your mask down.

00:08:37.717 --> 00:08:39.251
You take a bite.

00:08:39.251 --> 00:08:43.422
Then you put your mask back on,
you chew, swallow, then repeat.

00:08:43.422 --> 00:08:44.856
Or you could just
fill your mask with food

00:08:44.856 --> 00:08:46.025
and eat like a horse.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.463
Even Donald Trump was like...

00:08:53.266 --> 00:08:54.666
"Whaaat?"

00:08:54.666 --> 00:08:56.335
This is interesting.

00:08:56.335 --> 00:08:57.603
I saw that,
starting in November,

00:08:57.603 --> 00:09:01.440
Singapore will
offer cruises to nowhere.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:02.774
So they're basically
just going to go out,

00:09:02.774 --> 00:09:04.910
float, and come back.

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:06.845
So if you're tired of
being cooped up at home,

00:09:06.845 --> 00:09:11.049
try it in a smaller room
that rocks back and forth.

00:09:11.049 --> 00:09:12.985
Normally, if someone invites you
on a cruise to nowhere,

00:09:12.985 --> 00:09:14.219
you're like "Okay, cool.

00:09:14.219 --> 00:09:16.288
I'm about to be murdered."

00:09:16.288 --> 00:09:18.124
Seriously, I'm pretty sure
"Cruise to Nowhere"

00:09:18.124 --> 00:09:20.792
is the name of
every "Dateline" episode.

00:09:20.792 --> 00:09:23.395
"They had the perfect marriage.

00:09:23.395 --> 00:09:28.567
Then they booked two tickets on
a cruise...to nowhere."

00:09:28.567 --> 00:09:29.701
Speaking of traveling,

00:09:29.701 --> 00:09:32.137
I saw that hotels.com
is offering a stay

00:09:32.137 --> 00:09:34.072
in a pretty
interesting destination.

00:09:34.072 --> 00:09:38.143 line:0%
-Hotels.com
is offering a unique escape.

00:09:38.143 --> 00:09:41.380 line:0%
After casting your early ballot,
you can enter a contest

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:44.350 line:0%
to live under a rock
during election week.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:47.586 line:0%
It's a man-made cave
built 50 feet below ground.

00:09:47.586 --> 00:09:50.456
-The website's great.

00:09:50.456 --> 00:09:52.425
It's like, "Oh, we got
a king-sized bed.

00:09:52.425 --> 00:09:56.696
You got a Jacuzzi, mole people."

00:09:56.696 --> 00:09:58.464
And, finally,
a café in Prague is getting

00:09:58.464 --> 00:09:59.731
a lot of attention
for its new dessert.

00:09:59.731 --> 00:10:01.066
Check it out.

00:10:01.066 --> 00:10:03.536 line:0%
-There's a café in Prague which
is looking to, well,

00:10:03.536 --> 00:10:06.104 line:0%
lighten the mood amid
a slump in business

00:10:06.104 --> 00:10:07.473 line:0%
because of the pandemic.

00:10:07.473 --> 00:10:10.009 line:0%
Owners debuted
a dessert cake shaped

00:10:10.009 --> 00:10:13.846 line:0%
like the novel coronavirus
in an effort to draw customers.

00:10:13.846 --> 00:10:16.715
-Yeah, they're really into
the whole theme.

00:10:16.715 --> 00:10:18.584
When you order it,
the server puts it in his mouth

00:10:18.584 --> 00:10:22.088
and spits it back
into yours like a baby bird.

